    {
        "content": "<p>I found the problem. The parser for <code>lean</code> blocks in <code>VersoBlog</code> parses, for the first such block in a file, the whole preceding contents of the file as whitespace belonging to the first syntax leaf. That is because of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/commit/35944c367b9468fc49ac57aa321e9dd69fa9b586\">this</a> change to the module parser of Lean. That change is not yet reflected <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/verso/blob/86494197017df60fb4a30a6637294426e6d17a7f/src/verso-blog/VersoBlog.lean#L483\">here</a> (<code>hasLeading := false</code> has to be added to <code>state</code> there). I will make a PR tomorrow, after testing one more thing.</p>",
        "id": 609723893,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Miele",
        "timestamp": 1783892170
    },
